  "lineage": "The most common North Indian Hindustani classical vocal genre, replacing dhrupad as the dominant vocal form from the 18th century onward — codified through the Gwalior, Agra, Kirana, Patiala, Atrauli-Jaipur gharana lineages; characterized by the bilampat-laya-vilambit-laya (slow tempo) opening composition (cheez or bandish) followed by improvisation through alap, bol-banav (word-elaboration), tan (rapid melodic runs), and laykari (rhythmic variation)",
